    "established": [
      "Generic pivotal, spherical, balancing, and ribbon contracts remain established as typed Lean interfaces.",
      "The Drinfeld morphism is the unique right-dual comparison whose forward map expands exactly to EGNO equation (8.30).",
      "The Drinfeld morphism is objectwise invertible by uniqueness of right duals.",
      "The cup-crossing-cap formula is natural: the Lean proof uses braiding naturality and the evaluation and coevaluation mate identities.",
      "The Drinfeld components assemble into a natural isomorphism from the identity functor to the chosen right double-dual functor.",
      "Composing the ribbon twist with the Drinfeld natural isomorphism gives the canonical pivotal candidate as a natural isomorphism, matching EGNO equation (8.35) objectwise.",
      "Six mutation tests reject the Step 1 convention errors, a missing naturality witness, hom-only components without inverses, and replacement of f** by f*.",
      "The right double-dual functor now requires only RightRigidCategory, and a no-braiding regression module prevents reintroduction of the right-left-right instance diamond."
    ],
    "explicit_non_claims": [
      "This objective note is not a theorem claim.",
